# Customer Intelligence validation (the directive of 2026-11-09, Phase 9; the owner's word of 13:0x UTC: "you can do Validation"). Written by the implementer: the model-dependent half of the list — where the customer's own words place them, the money the writer quotes must follow, and the details must be captured. The model-free half runs in CI (test_geography*, test_insights*, test_timeline*, test_segments). Reported separately from the independent and blind sets.
{"id": "cint-001", "source": "developer", "categories": ["simple-enquiry", "memory", "cultural"], "lang": "en", "country": "BH", "critical": true, "notes": "The Bahrain/Kenya case. A +973 number is quoted in dollars until they say Nairobi; from that turn the market is Kenya: the location is captured, the quote is restated in shillings, and the next turn stays in shillings without being asked where they are.", "turns": [{"user": "Hi, how much is a clergy shirt?", "expect": {"next": "quote", "figures": "hub-only", "require": ["\\$|USD"], "forbid": ["\\bKES\\b|\\bKsh"]}}, {"user": "I'm in Nairobi, Westlands. Can you deliver here?", "expect": {"next": "answer", "tool": "capture_customer", "require": ["\\bKES\\b|\\bKsh"], "forbid": ["which country", "where are you", "are you in kenya"], "figures": "hub-only"}}, {"user": "And the cassock?", "expect": {"next": "quote", "figures": "hub-only", "require": ["\\bKES\\b|\\bKsh"], "forbid": ["\\$|USD"]}}]}
{"id": "cint-002", "source": "developer", "categories": ["simple-enquiry", "memory"], "lang": "en", "country": "KE", "critical": true, "notes": "The reverse: a Kenyan number whose owner has moved to Dubai. Their words outrank the number: the location is captured and the next quote is in dollars, not shillings.", "turns": [{"user": "Hello, I'm in Dubai now. Do you ship to the UAE?", "expect": {"next": "answer", "tool": "capture_customer", "forbid": ["which country", "where are you"]}}, {"user": "How much is a stole then?", "expect": {"next": "quote", "figures": "hub-only", "require": ["\\$|USD"], "forbid": ["\\bKES\\b|\\bKsh"]}}]}
{"id": "cint-003", "source": "developer", "categories": ["simple-enquiry", "memory"], "lang": "en", "country": "KE", "critical": false, "notes": "A Kenyan number naming a Kenyan town: the town is captured (city on the record), the market does not move, nobody is asked where they are.", "turns": [{"user": "Niko Nakuru. How much is a communion set?", "expect": {"next": "quote", "tool": "capture_customer", "figures": "hub-only", "require": ["\\bKES\\b|\\bKsh"], "forbid": ["\\$|USD", "which town", "where are you"]}}]}
{"id": "cint-004", "source": "developer", "categories": ["simple-enquiry", "memory", "cultural"], "lang": "en", "country": "UG", "critical": false, "notes": "A Ugandan number naming Kampala: captured as their location; the market stays dollars (the hub prices no shillings for Uganda), and the writer does not call them Kenyan or quote shillings.", "turns": [{"user": "Good morning. I'm in Kampala, I need prices for chasubles.", "expect": {"next": "quote", "tool": "capture_customer", "figures": "hub-only", "require": ["\\$|USD"], "forbid": ["\\bKES\\b|\\bKsh", "m-?pesa"]}}]}
{"id": "cint-005", "source": "developer", "categories": ["closing", "needs-silence"], "lang": "en", "country": "KE", "critical": false, "notes": "A hold the floor reads (needs_time): accepted without a reminder question; the timeline line and the hold on the deal are written model-free (test_timeline_db); here the reply itself is checked.", "turns": [{"user": "How much is a cassock?", "expect": {"next": "quote", "figures": "hub-only"}}, {"user": "Let me think about it and get back to you next week.", "expect": {"said": "needs_time", "next": "hold_ack", "forbid": ["remind you", "check back", "which day", "\\?"], "require": ["cassock"]}}]}
{"id": "cint-006", "source": "developer", "categories": ["payment"], "lang": "en", "country": "KE", "critical": true, "notes": "A payment claim with nothing in the hub: never thanked as paid; the hub is checked. The snapshot's next best action (verify the payment) is model-free; here the reply is checked.", "turns": [{"user": "How much is a clergy collar?", "expect": {"next": "quote", "figures": "hub-only"}}, {"user": "I have paid, please send it", "expect": {"said": "paid_claim", "next": "confirm_paid_check", "tool": "check_order_status", "forbid": ["thank you for (the|your) payment", "payment received", "we have received"]}}]}
